(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m3"] = E["hr-m3"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-3-1"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-3-1-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-1","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Opening the interview","tr":"Mülakatı açmak","fa":"شروع مصاحبه"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can open an interview: welcome the candidate and explain the plan and the timing.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir mülakatı açabileceksin: adayı karşılayıp planı ve süreyi açıklayabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی مصاحبه را شروع کنی: به متقاضی خوشامد بگویی و برنامه و زمان‌بندی را توضیح بدهی."},"hook":{"en":"Give the plan before the first question. A candidate who knows what comes next can show their best. Omar wanted to skip it. Leyla took one minute to show the plan, and Deniz put his pen down.","tr":"İlk sorudan önce planı söyle. Sırada ne olduğunu bilen aday en iyi hâlini gösterebilir. Omar bu kısmı atlamak istedi. Leyla planı göstermek için bir dakika ayırdı ve Deniz kalemini bıraktı.","fa":"قبل از اولین سؤال برنامه را بگو. متقاضی‌ای که می‌داند بعد چه می‌شود، بهتر می‌تواند توانایی‌اش را نشان بدهد. عمر می‌خواست این قسمت را رد کند. لیلا یک دقیقه وقت گذاشت تا برنامه را نشان دهد و دنیز خودکارش را زمین گذاشت."},"before":{"en":"Write a short interview invitation: when and where, who is joining, what happens and when it ends.","tr":"Kısa bir görüşme daveti yaz: ne zaman ve nerede, kimler katılıyor, neler olacak ve ne zaman bitecek.","fa":"یک دعوت‌نامه‌ی کوتاه مصاحبه بنویس: کی و کجا، چه کسانی هستند، چه اتفاقی می‌افتد و کی تمام می‌شود."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"5"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Give the plan before the first question","tr":"İlk sorudan önce planı söyle","fa":"قبل از اولین سؤال برنامه را بگو"},"body":{"en":"A candidate who knows the plan can think about the answers, not the clock. So say who is here, what happens and when it ends.","tr":"Planı bilen aday saate değil, cevaplarına odaklanır. Bu yüzden kimlerin olduğunu, neler olacağını ve ne zaman biteceğini söyle.","fa":"متقاضی‌ای که برنامه را می‌داند، به جواب‌ها فکر می‌کند نه به ساعت. پس بگو چه کسانی در جلسه هستند، چه اتفاقی می‌افتد و کی تمام می‌شود."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Future forms for the interview plan","tr":"Mülakat planı için gelecek zaman biçimleri","fa":"شکل‌های آینده برای برنامه‌ی مصاحبه"},"steps":[{"en":"Fixed with other people: present continuous.","tr":"Başkalarıyla ayarlanmış: present continuous.","fa":"برای قراری که با دیگران هماهنگ شده، حال استمراری می‌آید.","ex":"Omar is joining us on video at 10:30."},{"en":"Your own plan, decided before: am/is/are going to.","tr":"Önceden karar verdiğin kendi planın: am/is/are going to.","fa":"برای برنامه‌ای که خودت از قبل تصمیمش را گرفته‌ای، am/is/are going to می‌آید.","ex":"I'm going to ask you about your past jobs."},{"en":"Steps you announce now, and promises: will + bare verb.","tr":"Şimdi duyurduğun adımlar ve sözler: will + yalın fiil.","fa":"برای مرحله‌هایی که همین حالا اعلام می‌کنی و برای قول‌ها، will و فعل ساده می‌آید.","ex":"First I'll explain the role. We'll finish by eleven."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Job","Pattern"],"tr":["İşlev","Kalıp"],"fa":["کاربرد","الگو"]},"rows":[["Fixed arrangement with others","Omar is joining us at 10:30."],["Your plan, decided before","I'm going to ask you about your past jobs."],["Steps you announce now","First I'll explain the role, then you'll have time for questions."],["Finish time (promise)","We'll finish by eleven."]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish and Persian use one present or future form for all three (katılıyor / katılacak; mi-ayad / khahad amad). English chooses by who decided and when.","tr":"Türkçede üçü için de çoğu zaman 'katılıyor' ya da 'katılacak' yeter. İngilizcede seçim kimin, ne zaman karar verdiğine bağlıdır: is joining, going to, will.","fa":"در فارسی برای هر سه معمولاً «می‌آید» یا «خواهد آمد» کافی است. در انگلیسی انتخاب به این بستگی دارد که چه کسی و کی تصمیم گرفته: is joining، going to، ⁨will⁩."},"wrong":"Omar joins us on video at 10:30.","right":"Omar is joining us on video at 10:30."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"Let me explain how today is going to work.","meaning":{"en":"Opens the explanation of the process.","tr":"Sürecin açıklamasını başlatır.","fa":"توضیح روند مصاحبه را شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"First I'll..., then you'll have a chance to...","meaning":{"en":"Gives the order of the steps.","tr":"Adımların sırasını verir.","fa":"ترتیب مرحله‌ها را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"Feel free to take a moment.","meaning":{"en":"Gives the candidate permission to think.","tr":"Adaya düşünme izni verir.","fa":"به متقاضی اجازه می‌دهد کمی فکر کند."}},{"phrase":"overview","meaning":{"en":"A short description of the main points.","tr":"genel bakış.","fa":"نمای کلی؛ خلاصه‌ی نکته‌های اصلی"}},{"phrase":"join","meaning":{"en":"To take part in a meeting or call.","tr":"(görüşmeye) katılmak.","fa":"به جلسه یا تماس پیوستن؛ حضور پیدا کردن"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Candidates expect the plan","tr":"Adaylar planı duymak ister","fa":"متقاضی انتظار دارد برنامه را بداند"},"body":{"en":"In many UK and US interviews, the interviewer explains the structure and timing at the start, and candidates expect it. In some workplaces in Turkey, Iran and the Persian Gulf, an interview may begin straight with questions or with a longer general chat. Explaining the structure helps everyone, and it helps most when the candidate is speaking a second language.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan mülakatında görüşmeci başta yapıyı ve süreyi açıklar ve adaylar bunu bekler. Türkiye, İran ve Basra Körfezi'ndeki bazı işyerlerinde mülakat doğrudan sorularla ya da daha uzun genel bir sohbetle başlayabilir. Yapıyı açıklamak herkese yardımcı olur, en çok da aday ikinci bir dilde konuşuyorsa.","fa":"در بسیاری از مصاحبه‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، مصاحبه‌گر در همان ابتدا ساختار و زمان‌بندی جلسه را توضیح می‌دهد و متقاضیان هم انتظارش را دارند. در بعضی محیط‌های کاری در ترکیه، ایران و کشورهای حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس، مصاحبه ممکن است بی‌مقدمه با سؤال شروع شود یا با یک گفتگوی کلیِ طولانی‌تر. توضیح دادن ساختار به همه کمک می‌کند، و بیشتر از همه به متقاضی‌ای که به زبان دومش صحبت می‌کند."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از شروع ناگهانی تا گفتن برنامه"},"text":"Facts: The plan: explain the role, ask about their work, finish by eleven.","item":"Okay. Tell me why you want this job.","why":{"en":"Weak: straight into questions. Strong: what happens, and when it ends.","tr":"Zayıf: doğrudan sorulara giriyor. Güçlü: neler olacağı ve ne zaman biteceği.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول مستقیم سراغ سؤال‌ها می‌رود. نسخه‌ی دوم می‌گوید چه اتفاقی می‌افتد و کی تمام می‌شود."},"answer":"Thank you for coming. First I'll explain the role, then I'll ask about your work. We'll finish by eleven.","cut":["Okay.","Tell me why you want this job."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap what starts the questions before the candidate knows the plan.","tr":"Aday planı öğrenmeden sorulara başlayan sözlere dokun.","fa":"روی حرف‌هایی بزن که قبل از اینکه داوطلب برنامه را بداند، سؤال‌ها را شروع می‌کنند."}},"quick":{"prompt":"In some workplaces an interview starts straight with questions. With an international candidate, what should you do?","options":["Explain the structure and timing first","Start with questions: it saves time","Ask how long they want to stay"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Explain the structure first: many candidates expect it, and it helps most when they are speaking a second language.","tr":"Önce yapıyı ve süreyi anlat: Birçok aday bunu bekler ve en çok ikinci bir dilde konuşan adaya yardımı olur.","fa":"اول ساختار و زمان‌بندی را توضیح بده: خیلی از داوطلب‌ها انتظارش را دارند و بیشتر از همه به کسی کمک می‌کند که به زبان دوم حرف می‌زند."},"point":4,"hint2":{"en":"Picture an interview in your second language with no idea how long it lasts. What would help you most at the start?","tr":"İkinci dilinde, ne kadar süreceğini bilmediğin bir görüşmeyi düşün. Başta sana en çok ne yardımcı olurdu?","fa":"مصاحبه‌ای را به زبان دومت تصور کن که نمی‌دانی چقدر طول می‌کشد. اول کار چه چیزی بیشتر از همه کمکت می‌کرد؟"}},"remember":{"en":"Is another person already in the calendar? Present continuous. Your own plan? going to. Saying it now? will. Result of this lesson: you can open an interview clearly. You also have an invitation email.","tr":"Başka biri zaten takvimde mi? Present continuous. Kendi planın mı? going to. Şimdi mi söylüyorsun? will. Bu dersin sonucu: bir mülakatı net biçimde açabilirsin ve elinde bir davet e-postası olur.","fa":"کس دیگری از قبل در تقویم هست؟ حال استمراری. برنامه‌ی خودت است؟ going to. همین حالا اعلامش می‌کنی؟ ⁨will⁩. حالا می‌توانی مصاحبه را روشن شروع کنی. ایمیل دعوت هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Future continuous for polite process talk","tr":"Kibar süreç anlatımı için future continuous","fa":"آینده‌ی استمراری برای توضیح مؤدبانه‌ی روند"},"steps":[{"en":"In progress at a future time: will be + -ing.","tr":"Gelecekte bir anda sürmekte olan: will be + -ing.","fa":"برای کاری که در زمانی در آینده در جریان است، will be و فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"At 10:45 we'll be looking at your past jobs."},{"en":"Part of the planned flow: softer than will + verb.","tr":"Planlanmış akışın parçası: will + fiilden daha yumuşak.","fa":"برای بخشی از برنامه‌ی از پیش چیده‌شده هم به کار می‌رود و از will و فعل ساده نرم‌تر است.","ex":"Omar will be taking notes."},{"en":"Ask about plans politely: Will you be + -ing?","tr":"Planları kibarca sor: Will you be + -ing?","fa":"برای پرسیدن مؤدبانه درباره‌ی برنامه‌ها، سؤال را با Will you be و فعل -ing‌دار بساز.","ex":"Will you be needing a parking space?"}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Use","Example"],"tr":["Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["In progress at a later time","At 10:45 we'll be looking at your past jobs."],["Polite description of the process","I'll be asking you about three situations."],["Soft question about plans","Will you be needing a parking space?"]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: use the future continuous at least once in your opening and once in your email (for example \"I'll be asking you about...\").","tr":"B2 yolu: açılışında ve e-postanda en az birer kez future continuous kullan (örneğin \"I'll be asking you about...\").","fa":"مسیر B2: دست‌کم یک بار در شروع مصاحبه و یک بار در ایمیلت از آینده‌ی استمراری استفاده کن (مثلاً «⁨I'll be asking you about...⁩»)."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-3-1-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-1","title":"Future forms for the interview plan","titleTr":"Mülakat planı için gelecek zaman biçimleri","exp":{"en":"An interview opening tells the candidate what will happen, so it is full of future forms, and each one has a job. Use the present continuous for an arrangement already fixed with other people: \"Omar is joining us on video at 10:30.\" Use going to for your own plan, decided before the meeting: \"I'm going to ask you about your past jobs.\" Use will for the steps you announce now and for promises: \"First I'll explain the role, then you'll have time for questions. We'll finish by eleven.\" After will, always use the base verb: \"you'll have\", never \"you'll having\" or \"you'll to have\". And going to needs am/is/are: \"I'm going to ask\", not \"I going to ask\".","tr":"Mülakat açılışı adaya ne olacağını anlatır, bu yüzden gelecek zaman biçimleriyle doludur ve her birinin ayrı bir işi vardır. Türkçede çoğu zaman tek bir ek (-ecek/-acak) yeterlidir; İngilizcede üç biçim kullanılır. Başkalarıyla önceden ayarlanmış bir plan için present continuous: \"Omar is joining us on video at 10:30.\" Toplantıdan önce kendi verdiğin karar için going to: \"I'm going to ask you about your past jobs.\" Şimdi duyurduğun adımlar ve sözler için will: \"First I'll explain the role, then you'll have time for questions. We'll finish by eleven.\" Will'den sonra fiil her zaman yalın hâldedir: \"you'll have\"; \"you'll having\" ya da \"you'll to have\" değil. Going to için de am/is/are gerekir: \"I'm going to ask\", \"I going to ask\" değil.","fa":"شروع مصاحبه به متقاضی می‌گوید قرار است چه اتفاقی بیفتد؛ برای همین پر از شکل‌های آینده است و هر کدام کار خودش را دارد. ما در فارسی معمولاً با همان زمان حال از آینده حرف می‌زنیم («ساعت ده‌ونیم عمر هم می‌آید»)، اما انگلیسی سه شکل جدا دارد. برای قراری که از قبل با دیگران گذاشته شده، حال استمراری (present continuous): «⁨Omar is joining us on video at 10:30.⁩» برای برنامه‌ای که خودت قبل از جلسه تصمیمش را گرفته‌ای، going to: «⁨I'm going to ask you about your past jobs.⁩» برای مرحله‌هایی که همین حالا اعلام می‌کنی و برای قول دادن، will: «⁨First I'll explain the role, then you'll have time for questions. We'll finish by eleven.⁩» بعد از will همیشه فعل ساده می‌آید: «you'll have»، نه «you'll having» و نه «you'll to have». going to هم بدون am/is/are نمی‌آید: «I'm going to ask»، نه «I going to ask»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Job","Pattern"],"tr":["İşlev","Kalıp"],"fa":["کاربرد","الگو"]},"rows":[["Fixed arrangement with others","Omar is joining us at 10:30."],["Your plan, decided before","I'm going to ask you about your past jobs."],["Steps you announce now","First I'll explain the role, then you'll have time for questions."],["Finish time (promise)","We'll finish by eleven."]]},"wrong":"Then you will having a chance to ask questions.","right":"Then you will have a chance to ask questions.","blank":{"sentence":"Omar ___ us on video at 10:30.","word":"is joining","distractors":["joining","is join"]},"wrong2":"I going to ask you about your past jobs.","right2":"I'm going to ask you about your past jobs.","blank2":{"sentence":"First I will explain the role, and then you ___ have time for your questions.","word":"will","distractors":["are","going to"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Omar wanted to skip it. Leyla took one minute to show the plan, and Deniz put his pen down.","tr":"Omar bu kısmı atlamak istedi. Leyla planı göstermek için bir dakika ayırdı ve Deniz kalemini bıraktı.","fa":"عمر می‌خواست این قسمت را رد کند. لیلا یک دقیقه وقت گذاشت تا برنامه را نشان دهد و دنیز خودکارش را زمین گذاشت."},"tryWhy":{"en":"is joining: it is an arrangement already fixed with Omar, so use the present continuous with is.","tr":"is joining: Omar'la önceden ayarlanmış bir plan; bu yüzden is ile present continuous kullan.","fa":"جواب is joining است: این قراری است که از قبل با عمر هماهنگ شده؛ پس حال استمراری با is می‌آید."},"rule":[{"en":"Fixed with other people: present continuous.","tr":"Başkalarıyla ayarlanmış: present continuous.","fa":"برای قراری که با دیگران هماهنگ شده، حال استمراری می‌آید.","ex":"Omar is joining us on video at 10:30."},{"en":"Your own plan, decided before: am/is/are going to.","tr":"Önceden karar verdiğin kendi planın: am/is/are going to.","fa":"برای برنامه‌ای که خودت از قبل تصمیمش را گرفته‌ای، am/is/are going to می‌آید.","ex":"I'm going to ask you about your past jobs."},{"en":"Steps you announce now, and promises: will + bare verb.","tr":"Şimdi duyurduğun adımlar ve sözler: will + yalın fiil.","fa":"برای مرحله‌هایی که همین حالا اعلام می‌کنی و برای قول‌ها، will و فعل ساده می‌آید.","ex":"First I'll explain the role. We'll finish by eleven."}],"test":{"en":"Is another person already in the calendar? Present continuous. Your own plan? going to. Saying it now? will.","tr":"Başka biri zaten takvimde mi? Present continuous. Kendi planın mı? going to. Şimdi mi söylüyorsun? will.","fa":"کس دیگری از قبل در تقویم هست؟ حال استمراری. برنامه‌ی خودت است؟ going to. همین حالا اعلامش می‌کنی؟ ⁨will⁩."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish and Persian use one present or future form for all three (katılıyor / katılacak; mi-ayad / khahad amad). English chooses by who decided and when.","tr":"Türkçede üçü için de çoğu zaman 'katılıyor' ya da 'katılacak' yeter. İngilizcede seçim kimin, ne zaman karar verdiğine bağlıdır: is joining, going to, will.","fa":"در فارسی برای هر سه معمولاً «می‌آید» یا «خواهد آمد» کافی است. در انگلیسی انتخاب به این بستگی دارد که چه کسی و کی تصمیم گرفته: is joining، going to، ⁨will⁩."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["will having","will to have","will to be","you'll having","you'll to","we'll having"],"fix":{"en":"After will use the bare verb: 'you'll have time for questions.'","tr":"will'den sonra yalın fiil kullan: 'you'll have time for questions.'","fa":"بعد از will فعل ساده بیاور: «⁨you'll have time for questions.⁩»"}},{"find":["i going to","we going to","he going to","she going to","omar going to"],"fix":{"en":"going to needs am, is or are: 'I'm going to ask you about your past jobs.'","tr":"going to, am, is ya da are ister: 'I'm going to ask you about your past jobs.'","fa":"going to به am، is یا are نیاز دارد: «⁨I'm going to ask you about your past jobs.⁩»"}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-3-1-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-1","title":"Future continuous for polite process talk","titleTr":"Kibar süreç anlatımı için future continuous","exp":{"en":"Experienced interviewers often use the future continuous (will be + -ing) to describe what will be happening during the interview and to ask softly about plans: \"I'll be asking you about three situations.\", \"Omar will be taking notes.\", \"Will you be needing a parking space?\" It sounds less like an order than will + verb, because it presents the action as part of a planned flow, not as a decision you are pushing on someone. The form is always will be + -ing: never \"will taking\" and never \"will be take\".","tr":"Deneyimli görüşmeciler mülakat sırasında ne olacağını anlatmak ve planları yumuşak bir şekilde sormak için çoğu zaman future continuous (will be + -ing) kullanır: \"I'll be asking you about three situations.\", \"Omar will be taking notes.\", \"Will you be needing a parking space?\" Will + fiilden daha az emir gibi durur, çünkü eylemi birine dayatılan bir karar olarak değil, planlanmış akışın bir parçası olarak sunar. Biçim her zaman will be + -ing'dir: \"will taking\" ya da \"will be take\" asla olmaz.","fa":"مصاحبه‌گرهای باتجربه اغلب از آینده‌ی استمراری (⁨future continuous⁩) یعنی ⁨will be⁩ + ⁨-ing⁩ استفاده می‌کنند؛ هم برای اینکه بگویند در طول مصاحبه چه چیزی در جریان خواهد بود، هم برای اینکه درباره‌ی برنامه‌های طرف مقابل با ملایمت سؤال کنند: «⁨I'll be asking you about three situations.⁩»، «⁨Omar will be taking notes.⁩» و «⁨Will you be needing a parking space?⁩» این شکل از ⁨will⁩ + فعل کمتر دستوری به نظر می‌رسد، چون کار را بخشی از روندی از پیش برنامه‌ریزی‌شده نشان می‌دهد، نه تصمیمی که به کسی تحمیل می‌کنی. ساختارش همیشه ⁨will be⁩ + ⁨-ing⁩ است: نه «⁨will taking⁩» و نه «⁨will be take⁩»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Use","Example"],"tr":["Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["In progress at a later time","At 10:45 we'll be looking at your past jobs."],["Polite description of the process","I'll be asking you about three situations."],["Soft question about plans","Will you be needing a parking space?"]]},"wrong":"Omar will taking notes during the interview.","right":"Omar will be taking notes during the interview.","blank":{"sentence":"During the interview, Omar ___ notes.","word":"will be taking","distractors":["will taking","will be take"]},"wrong2":"Will you be need a parking space?","right2":"Will you be needing a parking space?","blank2":{"sentence":"At 10:45 we ___ at your past jobs.","word":"will be looking","distractors":["will looking","are be looking"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: use the future continuous at least once in your opening and once in your email (for example \"I'll be asking you about...\").","tr":"B2 yolu: açılışında ve e-postanda en az birer kez future continuous kullan (örneğin \"I'll be asking you about...\").","fa":"مسیر B2: دست‌کم یک بار در شروع مصاحبه و یک بار در ایمیلت از آینده‌ی استمراری استفاده کن (مثلاً «⁨I'll be asking you about...⁩»)."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-3-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"At 11:00 I ___ you the warehouse.","options":["will showing","will be showing","will be show"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"will be showing: the future continuous describes what will be in progress at 11:00, a polite way to talk about the plan. 'Will showing' drops be, and 'will be show' drops -ing.","tr":"will be showing: future continuous saat 11:00'de sürmekte olacak şeyi anlatır; plan hakkında kibar bir konuşma biçimidir. 'Will showing' be'yi, 'will be show' -ing'i düşürür.","fa":"⁨will be showing⁩ درست است، چون آینده‌ی استمراری کاری را می‌گوید که ساعت ۱۱ در جریان است و برای حرف زدن از برنامه مؤدبانه است. ⁨will showing⁩ بدون ⁨be⁩ و ⁨will be show⁩ بدون ⁨-ing⁩ است."}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"'Omar will be taking notes.' The future continuous makes the plan sound like a calm flow, not an order.","tr":"'Omar will be taking notes.' Future continuous planı bir emir gibi değil, sakin bir akış gibi gösterir.","fa":"«⁨Omar will be taking notes.⁩» آینده‌ی استمراری برنامه را مثل یک روند آرام نشان می‌دهد، نه یک دستور."},"tryWhy":{"en":"will be looking: the form is always will be + -ing. 'will looking' has no be.","tr":"will be looking: yapı her zaman will be + -ing'dir. 'will looking'de be eksik.","fa":"جواب will be looking است: ساختار همیشه will be و فعل -ing‌دار است. در will looking کلمه‌ی be جا افتاده."},"rule":[{"en":"In progress at a future time: will be + -ing.","tr":"Gelecekte bir anda sürmekte olan: will be + -ing.","fa":"برای کاری که در زمانی در آینده در جریان است، will be و فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"At 10:45 we'll be looking at your past jobs."},{"en":"Part of the planned flow: softer than will + verb.","tr":"Planlanmış akışın parçası: will + fiilden daha yumuşak.","fa":"برای بخشی از برنامه‌ی از پیش چیده‌شده هم به کار می‌رود و از will و فعل ساده نرم‌تر است.","ex":"Omar will be taking notes."},{"en":"Ask about plans politely: Will you be + -ing?","tr":"Planları kibarca sor: Will you be + -ing?","fa":"برای پرسیدن مؤدبانه درباره‌ی برنامه‌ها، سؤال را با Will you be و فعل -ing‌دار بساز.","ex":"Will you be needing a parking space?"}],"test":{"en":"Count the parts: will, be, and a verb with -ing. All three? Correct.","tr":"Parçaları say: will, be ve -ing almış bir fiil. Üçü de var mı? Doğru.","fa":"بخش‌ها را بشمار: ⁨will⁩، ⁨be⁩ و یک فعل با ⁨-ing⁩. هر سه هست؟ درست است."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish -yor olacak ('not alıyor olacak') matches this form well. Persian has no single equivalent, so it often sounds unnecessary; in English it is the polite choice.","tr":"Türkçedeki '-yor olacak' (not alıyor olacak) bu yapıya çok yakındır. İngilizcede bu biçim, süreci anlatmanın kibar yoludur.","fa":"فارسی معادل دقیقی برای این ساختار ندارد و شاید زیادی به نظر برسد، اما در انگلیسی این شکل، راه مؤدبانه‌ی توضیح روند کار است: «⁨Omar will be taking notes.⁩»"}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["will taking","will looking","will asking","will be take","will be ask","will be need","will be look"],"fix":{"en":"The future continuous is will be + -ing: 'Omar will be taking notes.'","tr":"Future continuous, will be + -ing'dir: 'Omar will be taking notes.'","fa":"آینده‌ی استمراری یعنی will be و فعل -ing‌دار: «Omar will be taking notes.»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-3-1-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-1","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Opening an Interview","tr":"Mülakatı Açmak","fa":"شروع مصاحبه"},"cards":[{"word":"panel","sentence":"Omar and I are the interview panel today.","meaning":{"en":"A small group of people who interview together.","tr":"mülakat heyeti, panel.","fa":"هیئت مصاحبه (چند نفر که با هم مصاحبه می‌کنند)"}},{"word":"put someone at ease","sentence":"A warm welcome puts most candidates at ease.","gap":"puts most candidates at ease","accept":["puts most candidates at ease","put someone at ease"],"meaning":{"en":"To help someone feel relaxed.","tr":"birini rahatlatmak.","fa":"به کسی آرامش دادن؛ کاری کردن که راحت باشد"}},{"word":"overview","sentence":"Let me give you a short overview of the role.","meaning":{"en":"A short description of the main points.","tr":"genel bakış.","fa":"نمای کلی؛ خلاصه‌ی نکته‌های اصلی"}},{"word":"structure","sentence":"The interview has a simple structure: three parts.","meaning":{"en":"The way the parts of something are organised.","tr":"yapı, düzen.","fa":"ساختار؛ نحوه‌ی چیده شدن بخش‌ها"}},{"word":"feel free to","sentence":"Feel free to take a moment before you answer.","meaning":{"en":"You are welcome to do something.","tr":"çekinmeden ... yapabilirsin.","fa":"راحت باش و ...؛ اشکالی ندارد که ..."}},{"word":"have a chance to","sentence":"You'll have a chance to ask questions at the end.","meaning":{"en":"To have the time or opportunity to do something.","tr":"... fırsatı olmak.","fa":"فرصت ... را داشتن"}},{"word":"wrap up","sentence":"We'll wrap up by eleven.","meaning":{"en":"To finish a meeting or task.","tr":"toparlamak, bitirmek.","fa":"جمع‌بندی کردن و به پایان رساندن"}},{"word":"join","sentence":"Omar is joining us from Dubai on video.","gap":"joining","accept":["joining","join"],"meaning":{"en":"To take part in a meeting or call.","tr":"(görüşmeye) katılmak.","fa":"به جلسه یا تماس پیوستن؛ حضور پیدا کردن"}},{"word":"timing","sentence":"Before we start, let me explain the timing.","meaning":{"en":"When things happen and how long they take.","tr":"zamanlama.","fa":"زمان‌بندی"}},{"word":"hiring decision","sentence":"We'll make a hiring decision by Friday.","meaning":{"en":"The final choice about who gets the job.","tr":"işe alım kararı.","fa":"تصمیم نهایی استخدام"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-3-1-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-1","title":{"en":"The First Minute","tr":"İlk Dakika","fa":"دقیقه‌ی اول"},"text":"Omar joined the video call at 10:28, two minutes early, which for Omar meant he was in a hurry.\n\n\"Let's go straight to the questions,\" he said. \"I have a warehouse to run.\"\n\n\"Give me one minute at the start,\" Leyla said. \"Just one.\"\n\nDeniz came in at 10:30. He sat very straight and held a pen he did not need. On the screen, Omar looked at his watch.\n\nLeyla smiled. \"Welcome back, Deniz. Before we start, let me explain how today is going to work. Omar is joining us from Dubai, so you'll see him on the screen. First I'll give you a short overview of the role. Then I'm going to ask you about some real situations from your past jobs. After that, you'll have a chance to ask us anything. We'll finish by eleven.\"\n\n\"Okay,\" Deniz said. His shoulders came down a little.\n\n\"And feel free to take a moment before you answer. There's no rush.\"\n\nDeniz put the pen down.\n\nThe interview took twenty-five minutes. Deniz gave long, clear answers. When he left, Omar was quiet for a moment.\n\n\"That minute,\" he said at last. \"He knew where he was the whole time.\"\n\n\"That's the idea,\" Leyla said. \"When people can see the map, they stop looking for the exit.\"\n\nOmar laughed. \"Write that down. I'm going to use it in my own interviews.\"\n\nThat evening Deniz called his sister in Dubai. He could not remember all the questions. But he remembered one sentence: There's no rush.","vocab":[{"word":"in a hurry","en":"Wanting to do things fast.","tr":"acelesi olan","fa":"عجله داشتن؛ با عجله"},{"word":"straight","en":"Here: with the back very upright.","tr":"dimdik","fa":"صاف (نشستن با کمر صاف)"},{"word":"shoulders","en":"The top of the body, between neck and arms.","tr":"omuzlar","fa":"شانه‌ها"},{"word":"no rush","en":"You do not need to hurry.","tr":"acele yok","fa":"عجله‌ای نیست؛ سر فرصت"},{"word":"exit","en":"The way out.","tr":"çıkış","fa":"راه خروج"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why did Leyla want one minute at the start?","options":["To finish the interview early","To explain the plan so Deniz could relax","To let Omar arrive"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct sentence.","options":["Omar is join us from Dubai.","Omar joining us from Dubai.","Omar is joining us from Dubai."],"correct":2},{"prompt":"What did Omar decide to do after the interview?","options":["Use the same opening in his own interviews","Hire Deniz at once","Skip openings in the future"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Why did Deniz remember \"There's no rush\"?","options":["He thought it was a trick","It made him feel safe enough to think","He did not understand it"],"correct":1}],"notice":{"en":"Omar wants to skip the opening. Leyla asks for one minute. Watch what she says in it, and what changes in Deniz.","tr":"Omar girişi atlamak istiyor. Leyla bir dakika istiyor. O dakikada ne söylediğine ve Deniz'de neyin değiştiğine dikkat et.","fa":"عمر می‌خواهد شروع را رد کند. لیلا یک دقیقه وقت می‌خواهد. دقت کن در آن یک دقیقه چه می‌گوید و چه چیزی در دنیز عوض می‌شود."},"bridge":{"en":"In one minute Leyla used three future forms. Next: see which one does which job.","tr":"Leyla bir dakikada üç farklı gelecek zaman biçimi kullandı. Sırada: hangisinin ne işe yaradığını gör.","fa":"لیلا در یک دقیقه از سه شکل آینده استفاده کرد. قدم بعد: ببین هر کدام چه کار می‌کند."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-3-1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-1","topic":{"en":"Opening an Interview","tr":"Mülakatı Açmak","fa":"شروع مصاحبه"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of a time someone explained the plan before a stressful moment (a doctor, a teacher, an exam). How did it change how you felt?","tr":"Stresli bir andan önce birinin sana planı anlattığı bir zamanı düşün (doktor, öğretmen, sınav). Hissettiklerini nasıl değiştirdi?","fa":"یک بار را به یاد بیاور که کسی قبل از یک لحظه‌ی پراسترس (پیش پزشک، سر کلاس، قبل از امتحان) برنامه را برایت توضیح داد. حالت را چطور عوض کرد؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Welcome the candidate and introduce the panel: who is in the room and who is on the screen.","tr":"Adayı karşıla ve paneli tanıt: odada kim var, ekranda kim var.","fa":"به متقاضی خوشامد بگو و اعضای هیئت مصاحبه را معرفی کن: چه کسی در اتاق است و چه کسی پشت صفحه."},{"en":"Explain the three parts of the interview and the finish time. Use will, going to and the present continuous.","tr":"Mülakatın üç aşamasını ve bitiş saatini açıkla. Will, going to ve present continuous kullan.","fa":"سه بخش مصاحبه و ساعت پایان را توضیح بده. از will، going to و present continuous استفاده کن."},{"en":"Invite questions and tell the candidate it is fine to take a moment before answering.","tr":"Soru sormaya davet et ve cevap vermeden önce biraz düşünmenin sorun olmadığını söyle.","fa":"او را به پرسیدن سؤال دعوت کن و بگو اشکالی ندارد قبل از جواب دادن کمی فکر کند."}],"followups":[{"en":"Say the whole opening in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45. Keep all three parts each time.","tr":"Açılışın tamamını 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede söyle. Her seferinde üç aşamayı da koru.","fa":"کل این شروع را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه بگو. هر بار هر سه بخش را بگو."},{"en":"The candidate asks: \"How many people are you interviewing?\" Answer politely without giving names.","tr":"Aday soruyor: \"Kaç kişiyle mülakat yapıyorsunuz?\" İsim vermeden kibarca cevap ver.","fa":"متقاضی می‌پرسد: «⁨How many people are you interviewing?⁩» مؤدبانه جواب بده، بدون اینکه اسم کسی را بیاوری."},{"en":"Now open an interview for a real job at your company: the plan and the time.","tr":"Şimdi şirketindeki gerçek bir iş için mülakatı aç: plan ve süre.","fa":"حالا مصاحبه‌ی یک شغل واقعی در شرکتت را شروع کن: برنامه و زمان."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"Let me explain how today is going to work.","meaning":{"en":"Opens the explanation of the process.","tr":"Sürecin açıklamasını başlatır.","fa":"توضیح روند مصاحبه را شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"First I'll..., then you'll have a chance to...","meaning":{"en":"Gives the order of the steps.","tr":"Adımların sırasını verir.","fa":"ترتیب مرحله‌ها را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"Feel free to take a moment.","meaning":{"en":"Gives the candidate permission to think.","tr":"Adaya düşünme izni verir.","fa":"به متقاضی اجازه می‌دهد کمی فکر کند."}}],"culture":{"en":"In many UK and US interviews, the interviewer explains the structure and timing at the start, and candidates expect it. In some workplaces in Turkey, Iran and the Persian Gulf, an interview may begin straight with questions or with a longer general chat. Explaining the structure helps everyone, and it helps most when the candidate is speaking a second language.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan mülakatında görüşmeci başta yapıyı ve süreyi açıklar ve adaylar bunu bekler. Türkiye, İran ve Basra Körfezi'ndeki bazı işyerlerinde mülakat doğrudan sorularla ya da daha uzun genel bir sohbetle başlayabilir. Yapıyı açıklamak herkese yardımcı olur, en çok da aday ikinci bir dilde konuşuyorsa.","fa":"در بسیاری از مصاحبه‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، مصاحبه‌گر در همان ابتدا ساختار و زمان‌بندی جلسه را توضیح می‌دهد و متقاضیان هم انتظارش را دارند. در بعضی محیط‌های کاری در ترکیه، ایران و کشورهای حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس، مصاحبه ممکن است بی‌مقدمه با سؤال شروع شود یا با یک گفتگوی کلیِ طولانی‌تر. توضیح دادن ساختار به همه کمک می‌کند، و بیشتر از همه به متقاضی‌ای که به زبان دومش صحبت می‌کند."},"model":"Welcome, Deniz, and thank you for coming. Omar is joining us on video from Dubai. Let me explain how today is going to work. First I'll give you a short overview of the role. Then I'm going to ask you about some real situations from your past jobs. After that, you'll have a chance to ask us anything. We'll finish by eleven. Feel free to take a moment before you answer.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I introduced everyone in the room and on the screen.","tr":"Odadaki ve ekrandaki herkesi tanıttım.","fa":"همه‌ی کسانی را که در اتاق و پشت صفحه بودند معرفی کردم."},{"en":"I gave the three parts and the finish time.","tr":"Üç aşamayı ve bitiş saatini söyledim.","fa":"سه بخش مصاحبه و ساعت پایان را گفتم."},{"en":"I used is joining, going to and will, each for its own job.","tr":"is joining, going to ve will'in her birini kendi işi için kullandım.","fa":"is joining، going to و will را هر کدام برای کار خودش به کار بردم."},{"en":"I told the candidate it is fine to take a moment.","tr":"Adaya düşünmek için zaman alabileceğini söyledim.","fa":"به متقاضی گفتم اشکالی ندارد کمی فکر کند."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-3-1-w","title":{"en":"The interview invitation to Deniz","tr":"Deniz'e mülakat daveti","fa":"دعوت‌نامه‌ی مصاحبه برای دنیز"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-1","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Write the interview invitation email to Deniz (60-90 words): date, time and place, who is joining, the three parts of the interview, the finish time and one thing to bring.","tr":"Deniz'e mülakat davet e-postasını yaz (60-90 kelime): tarih, saat ve yer, kimin katılacağı, mülakatın üç aşaması, bitiş saati ve getirmesi gereken bir şey.","fa":"ایمیل دعوت به مصاحبه را برای دنیز بنویس (۶۰ تا ۹۰ کلمه): تاریخ، ساعت و محل، چه کسانی حضور دارند، سه بخش مصاحبه، ساعت پایان و یک چیز که باید همراهش بیاورد."},"model":"Dear Deniz, Thank you for your application. We would like to invite you to an interview on Thursday 19 March at 10:30 at our Istanbul office. Omar, our Dubai operations manager, is joining us on video. First I'll give you an overview of the role, and then I'm going to ask you about your past work. You'll have time for your own questions at the end. We'll finish by 11:00. Please bring your driving licence. Kind regards, Leyla Karimi","frame":"Dear ___, Thank you for ___. We would like to invite you to ___ on ___ at ___. ___ is joining us ___. First I'll ___, and then I'm going to ___. You'll have time for ___. We'll finish by ___. Please bring ___. Kind regards, ___","words":[{"word":"invite"},{"word":"overview"},{"word":"finish"}],"minWords":60,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: date, time, place, who joins, three parts, finish time, what to bring","Organised: invitation, arrangement, process, practical point, close","Language: present continuous for the arrangement; going to for your plan; will for the steps","Tone: warm and clear, no pressure"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: tarih, saat, yer, kimlerin katılacağı, üç aşama, bitiş saati, getirilecekler","Düzen: davet, ayarlama, süreç, pratik bilgi, kapanış","Dil: ayarlama için present continuous; planın için going to; adımlar için will","Üslup: sıcak ve net, baskı yok"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: تاریخ، ساعت، مکان، حاضران، سه بخش، ساعت پایان، چیزهایی که باید همراه بیاورد","نظم: دعوت، هماهنگی، روند، نکته‌ی عملی، پایان","زبان: حال استمراری برای قرار هماهنگ‌شده؛ going to برای برنامه‌ات؛ will برای مراحل","لحن: گرم و روشن، بدون فشار"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"Date, time and place","tr":"Tarih, saat ve yer","fa":"تاریخ، ساعت و مکان"},"find":["interview on","office","thursday","at 10"],"sample":"Thursday 19 March, 10:30, Istanbul office"},{"t":{"en":"Who is joining","tr":"Kimlerin katılacağı","fa":"اینکه چه کسانی هستند"},"find":["is joining","joining us","will join"],"sample":"Omar, Dubai operations manager, on video"},{"t":{"en":"The parts of the interview","tr":"Görüşmenin bölümleri","fa":"بخش‌های مصاحبه"},"find":["first","then","at the end","overview"],"sample":"an overview of the role; past work; your questions"},{"t":{"en":"The finish time","tr":"Bitiş saati","fa":"ساعت پایان"},"find":["finish by","finish at","until"],"sample":"finish by 11:00"},{"t":{"en":"One thing to bring","tr":"Getirmesi gereken bir şey","fa":"یک چیزی که باید بیاورد"},"find":["please bring","bring"],"sample":"driving licence"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-3-1-p","title":{"en":"Deniz, five minutes in","tr":"Mülakatın beşinci dakikasında Deniz","fa":"دنیز، پنج دقیقه بعد از شروع مصاحبه"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-1","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Deniz, five minutes into the interview. Write 2 sentences in first person: what in Leyla's opening calmed you down, and why?","tr":"Mülakatın beşinci dakikasındaki Deniz'sin. Birinci tekil şahısla 2 cümle yaz: Leyla'nın açılışında seni ne sakinleştirdi ve neden?","fa":"تو دنیز هستی و پنج دقیقه از مصاحبه گذشته است. از زبان خودت دو جمله بنویس: چه چیزی در شروع صحبت لیلا آرامت کرد و چرا؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-3-1-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-1","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-3-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Ms Clarke ___ the interview at 11:00 tomorrow.","options":["is joining","joins to","is join"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"is joining: a fixed arrangement for tomorrow takes the present continuous. 'Joins to' adds a wrong 'to', and 'is join' drops -ing.","tr":"is joining: yarın için kesinleşmiş bir düzenleme present continuous alır. 'Joins to' yanlış bir 'to' ekler; 'is join' -ing'i düşürür.","fa":"⁨is joining⁩ درست است، چون قرار قطعی برای فردا حال استمراری می‌خواهد. ⁨joins to⁩ یک ⁨to⁩ اضافه دارد و ⁨is join⁩ بدون ⁨-ing⁩ است."}},{"from":"hr-3-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"After the tour, you ___ meet two of our drivers.","options":["will","are","going to"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"will: it tells the candidate what happens next in the plan. 'Are meet' is wrong, and 'going to' needs 'are' before it.","tr":"will: adaya plana göre sırada ne olacağını söyler. 'Are meet' yanlıştır; 'going to' öncesinde 'are' ister.","fa":"will درست است، چون به داوطلب می‌گوید در برنامه بعداً چه می‌شود. are meet غلط است و going to قبلش are لازم دارد."},"hint2":{"en":"This is a step in your plan for today, not an arrangement in the calendar. Which future form do you use for the steps?","tr":"Bu, bugünkü planındaki bir adım; takvimdeki bir randevu değil. Adımlar için hangi gelecek zaman biçimini kullanırsın?","fa":"این یک قدم از برنامه‌ی امروزت است، نه قراری که در تقویم ثبت شده. برای قدم‌ها از کدام شکل آینده استفاده می‌کنی؟"}},{"from":"hr-3-1","kind":"mcq","prompt":"You open an interview: \"Welcome, Deniz. Omar is joining us from Dubai. We'll talk about your past driving jobs, and then you can ask us anything.\" What is still missing from the plan?","options":["When the interview ends","Who is taking part","What will happen"],"correct":0,"point":1,"why":{"en":"When the interview ends: the opening says who is taking part (Omar) and what will happen (the driving jobs, then questions), but not when it finishes. One more line does it: \"We'll be done in about forty minutes.\"","tr":"When the interview ends: Açılış konuşman kimin katıldığını (Omar) ve neler olacağını (şoförlük işleri, ardından sorular) söylüyor, ama görüşmenin ne zaman biteceğini söylemiyor. Bir cümle daha yeter: \"We'll be done in about forty minutes.\"","fa":"«⁨When the interview ends⁩» درست است: در شروع مصاحبه گفته‌ای چه کسی در جلسه است (عمر) و چه اتفاقی می‌افتد (اول سابقه‌ی کارش در رانندگی، بعد سؤال‌ها)، ولی نگفته‌ای مصاحبه کی تمام می‌شود. یک جمله‌ی دیگر کافی است: «⁨We'll be done in about forty minutes.⁩»"},"hint2":{"en":"A candidate needs to know three things before the first question. Go through your opening line by line and tick off each one you can find.","tr":"Aday, ilk sorudan önce üç şeyi bilmeli. Açılış cümlelerini tek tek oku ve bulduğun her birini işaretle.","fa":"متقاضی قبل از اولین سؤال باید سه چیز را بداند. جمله‌های شروعت را یکی‌یکی بخوان و هر کدام را که پیدا کردی علامت بزن."}},{"from":"hr-2-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"Deniz is ___ experienced than Karim.","options":["more","most","much"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"more: a long adjective like experienced takes 'more ... than'. 'Most' compares three or more, and 'much' alone can't compare.","tr":"more: experienced gibi uzun bir sıfat 'more ... than' alır. 'Most' üç ve daha fazlasını karşılaştırır; tek başına 'much' karşılaştırma yapmaz.","fa":"more درست است، چون صفت بلندی مثل experienced با more ... than می‌آید. most برای سه یا بیشتر است و much تنها مقایسه نمی‌کند."}},{"from":"hr-2-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"We want people ___ take pride in safe driving.","options":["which","who","whose"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"who: it refers to people. 'Which' is for things, and 'whose' shows ownership.","tr":"who: insanları anlatır. 'Which' şeyler içindir; 'whose' sahiplik gösterir.","fa":"who درست است، چون به آدم‌ها برمی‌گردد. which برای چیزهاست و whose مالکیت را نشان می‌دهد."},"hint2":{"en":"The gap joins people to what they do. Which word starts a clause about people?","tr":"Boşluk insanları yaptıkları şeye bağlıyor. İnsanlarla ilgili bir yan cümleyi hangi kelime başlatır?","fa":"جای خالی آدم‌ها را به کاری که می‌کنند وصل می‌کند. کدام کلمه جمله‌ای درباره‌ی آدم‌ها را شروع می‌کند؟"}},{"from":"hr-1-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"This month Leyla ___ on the Dubai hiring plan.","options":["works","is working","work"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"is working: 'this month' is a temporary project, so is + -ing. 'Works' is a routine, and 'work' doesn't agree with Leyla.","tr":"is working: 'this month' geçici bir projedir, bu yüzden is + -ing. 'Works' rutindir; 'work' Leyla ile uyuşmaz.","fa":"is working درست است، چون this month پروژه‌ی موقتی است و is و فعل ing‌دار لازم است. works برنامه‌ی همیشگی است و work با Leyla جور نیست."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
